{"id":5015,"date":"2018-10-20T14:56:12","date_gmt":"2018-10-20T18:56:12","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=5015"},"modified":"2018-10-30T18:11:45","modified_gmt":"2018-10-30T22:11:45","slug":"volunteering-at-albuquerque-international-balloon-fiesta-aibf","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2018\/10\/20\/volunteering-at-albuquerque-international-balloon-fiesta-aibf\/","title":{"rendered":"Volunteering at Albuquerque International Balloon Fiesta (AIBF)"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><strong>UPDATE<\/strong>: <em>It&#8217;s October 30th, 2018.\u00a0 We left Albuquerque on Oct 9th, attended the RV Nomads Rally in Wellington, TX followed by the Texas Country Air(stream) Rally in Brownwood, TX then to Lake Colorado City State Park (TX) and now we are at Bottomless Lake State Park at Roswell, NM for a couple nights.\u00a0 We are on our way to our winter home at Rover&#8217;s Roost RV Park (Casa Grande, AZ)<\/em><\/p>\n<p>We just crossed the two year mark as full-time RV&#8217;ers. We&#8217;ve sold our Sticks n Bricks house in Ohio and lived virtually rent-free by Workamping our way around the country.<\/p>\n<p>As Workampers, we stay at RV parks, campgrounds, and other places for free in exchange for (generally) about 12-20 hours per week working at the park or campground.<\/p>\n<p>Very often parks and campgrounds want to bring on Workampers for the entire season .. usually 5 or 6 month stints.<\/p>\n<p>We started the full-time RV lifestyle to see the country and soon realized that if we only move twice a year &#8230; or go back to the same place twice &#8230; then we&#8217;ll be about 130 years old by the time we see all the places we want to go!<\/p>\n<p>As a result, we&#8217;ve been looking for shorter term gigs. That&#8217;s how we came to volunteer at Albuquerque International Balloon Fiesta (AIBF). We met our new good friends Matt and Sherry last winter at the Escapees RV Club &#8220;Rainbows End&#8221; park in Livingston, TX while we were all Workamping there.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_5025\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-5025\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption alignnone\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-5025 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180323_0933262154598183724253384.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180323_0933262154598183724253384.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180323_0933262154598183724253384-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180323_0933262154598183724253384-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180323_0933262154598183724253384-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-5025\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Matt &amp; Sherry Hylbom &#8220;Get Out The Map&#8221;<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>Matt and Sherry shared with us their experiences the previous fall working at the AIBF and it sounded exciting to us, so we reached out to the contact they gave us and here we are!<\/p>\n<p>We arrived a full 3 weeks before the start of Fiesta, and we spent that time; chalking boundaries of all the 1600 RV parking spaces, stringing flag lines around the perimeter lines of each of the 40 or so parking areas, setting up the volunteer break tent with tables, chairs, fridge and freezer, and getting the check-in booth all ready to greet and register the soon- to-be arriving RV&#8217;ers.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_5028\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-5028\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180925_161239.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-5028 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180925_161239.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180925_161239.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180925_161239-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180925_161239-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180925_161239-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-5028\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Early on, before the show begins &#8230; stormy weather can be seen obscuring the Sandia Mountains &#8211; See the rainbow just over the bed of the pickup?<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<figure id=\"attachment_5029\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-5029\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180926_150121.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-5029 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180926_150121.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180926_150121.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180926_150121-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180926_150121-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180926_150121-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-5029\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Of the 1600 spaces, about 400 had water and 30 amp electric. Electricians ran all the electric, but volunteers ran all the water lines<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<figure id=\"attachment_5030\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-5030\" style=\"width: 576px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181008_093321.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-5030 size-large\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181008_093321-e1540820372101-576x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"576\" height=\"1024\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181008_093321-e1540820372101-576x1024.jpg 576w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181008_093321-e1540820372101-169x300.jpg 169w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181008_093321-e1540820372101-768x1365.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181008_093321-e1540820372101.jpg 304w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 576px) 100vw, 576px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-5030\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">As one of the 1100 Navigators (Volunteers), we both got these snappy jackets!<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<figure id=\"attachment_5032\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-5032\" style=\"width: 2560px\" class=\"wp-caption aligncenter\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181015_105423.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-5032 size-full\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181015_105423.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"2560\" height=\"1440\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181015_105423.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181015_105423-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181015_105423-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181015_105423-1024x576.jpg 1024w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 2560px) 100vw, 2560px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-5032\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Most of the south lot is dirt, some gravel and even some old asphalt. Dusty week for sure with all those rigs coming and going!<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>And then the fun begins!<\/p>\n<p>Kathy worked 6 hour shifts at the check-in booth as RV&#8217;s pulled in to the lot (room for 1600 rigs). There are 3 windows at the booth so she worked with two other ladies each shift. They checked in the arrivals and gave them their parking passes and each rig also received a &#8220;goody bag&#8221; with some small gifts and lots of printed information about the event and the grounds.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_5034\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-5034\" style=\"width: 300px\" class=\"wp-caption alignright\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181006_081133.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-5034 size-medium\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181006_081133-300x169.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181006_081133-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181006_081133-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181006_081133-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20181006_081133.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-5034\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">The Check-In booth where Kathy and the other ladies worked<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>My primary responsibility was to stand at the head of the line and greet RV&#8217;ers pulling up, ask them to check-in at the booth, and then once they had their parking credentials, point them in the direction of a &#8220;parker&#8221; driving a golf cart who would then take them to their spot.<\/p>\n<figure id=\"attachment_5036\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-5036\" style=\"width: 300px\" class=\"wp-caption alignleft\"><a href=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/HerbParking.jpg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"size-medium wp-image-5036\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/HerbParking-300x200.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"300\" height=\"200\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/HerbParking-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/HerbParking.jpg 630w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/a><figcaption id=\"caption-attachment-5036\" class=\"wp-caption-text\">Pix published in the Albuquerque Journal<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n<p>&nbsp;<\/p>\n<p>Our work day started at 7:30 am when we all met in the volunteer tent and had a short meeting about what size crowd we could expect that day.\u00a0 Since everyone had reservations, we knew what groups were coming in and which ones were leaving on any given day.<\/p>\n<p>Although some stayed for the entire 10 day event, many came just for one or the other of the weekends.<\/p>\n<p>Rigs would be lined up in the drive from the night before and we parked all day until closing at 7:00 pm.\u00a0 Any arrivals after that time dry camped in the entrance drive until the next morning.<\/p>\n<p>Although we worked a LOT of hours during the 10 day Fiesta, we did have an opportunity (3 times) to take the shuttle bus across Alameda Avenue to the launch field to see the balloons.\u00a0 We went once in the morning to see the daily &#8220;Mass Ascension&#8221; and twice in the evening to see the &#8220;Glowdeo&#8221;.\u00a0 It was also great to be able to see the balloons land right in our RV parking lot occasionally!<\/p>\n<p>Here&#8217;s a slide show of some of the pictures I took.\u00a0 If you want to see ALL of the pictures, then go ahead and <a href=\"https:\/\/photos.app.goo.gl\/Tjn2HQeBpHmpn5VW9\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">follow this link to a Google Photo Album<\/a>\u00a0I put together.<\/p>\n<div id='gallery-1' class='gallery galleryid-5015 gallery-columns-2 gallery-size-medium'><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180922_090137.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180922_090137-300x169.jpg\" class=\"attachment-medium size-medium\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-5039\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180922_090137-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180922_090137-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180922_090137-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180922_090137.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-5039'>\n\t\t\t\tA pancake breakfast for the volunteers\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180923_142155.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180923_142155-300x169.jpg\" class=\"attachment-medium size-medium\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-5040\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180923_142155-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180923_142155-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180923_142155-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180923_142155.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-5040'>\n\t\t\t\tKathy and me in front of the Balloon Museum\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180923_150306.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180923_150306-300x169.jpg\" class=\"attachment-medium size-medium\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-5041\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180923_150306-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180923_150306-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180923_150306-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180923_150306.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-5041'>\n\t\t\t\tInside view of the Balloon Museum\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180924_132428.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180924_132428-300x169.jpg\" class=\"attachment-medium size-medium\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-5042\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180924_132428-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180924_132428-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180924_132428-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180924_132428.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-5042'>\n\t\t\t\tOur 450 hp 6 cyl diesel power generator for the volunteers\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180925_120053.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180925_120053-300x169.jpg\" class=\"attachment-medium size-medium\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-5043\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180925_120053-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180925_120053-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180925_120053-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180925_120053.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<figcaption class='wp-caption-text gallery-caption' id='gallery-1-5043'>\n\t\t\t\tThe &#8220;Poop Team&#8221; working with the pump truck to drain our waste tanks (twice weekly)\n\t\t\t\t<\/figcaption><\/figure><figure class='gallery-item'>\n\t\t\t<div class='gallery-icon landscape'>\n\t\t\t\t<a href='https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180927_165020.jpg'><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"169\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180927_165020-300x169.jpg\" class=\"attachment-medium size-medium\" alt=\"\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-5044\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180927_165020-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180927_165020-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180927_165020-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/10\/20180927_165020.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/a>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t